{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P17794","uniProtkbId":"VIRB4_AGRFC","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1990-08-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-11-04","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2002-03-27","entryVersion":131,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":3.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Agrobacterium fabrum (strain C58 / ATCC 33970)","commonName":"Agrobacterium tumefaciens (strain C58)","taxonId":176299,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Alphaproteobacteria","Hyphomicrobiales","Rhizobiaceae","Rhizobium/Agrobacterium group","Agrobacterium","Agrobacterium tumefaciens complex"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Type IV secretion system ATPase VirB4"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8152380"}],"value":"3.6.4.6"}]}},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2194232"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2233252"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2370849"}],"value":"virB4"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"value":"Atu6170"}],"orfNames":[{"value":"AGR_pTi_8"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P0A3W0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15668378"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8152380"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"12177443"}],"value":"Component of the VirB/VirD4 type IV secretion system (T4SS), which translocates transfer DNA (T-DNA) and virulence effector proteins into plant host cells, leading to crown gall disease (Probable). The VirB4 subunit is essential for virulence (PubMed:8152380). It provides energy for pilus biogenesis and substrate transfer (PubMed:15668378, PubMed:8152380). It shows ATPase activity (PubMed:8152380). It can act as a dislocation motor to catalyze extraction of VirB2 pilin monomers from the inner membrane during T4SS biogenesis, probably through ATP binding/hydrolysis, and acts synergistically with VirB11 to induce a structural change in the pilin (By similarity). It is required for T-DNA transfer (PubMed:8152380). May act as a docking site at the entrance of the T4SS channel and act in concert with VirD4 and VirB11 to transport substrates through the T4SS (PubMed:15668378)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13065"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"ecNumber":"3.6.4.6","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8152380"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13066"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8152380"}]}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"O50330"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15668378"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17038312"}],"value":"The core secretion machinery of the VirB/VirD4 T4SS is composed of cytoplasmic ATPases that form the energy center, an inner membrane complex (IMC), an outer membrane core complex (OMCC) and a stalk (or cylinder) that connects the IMC and the OMCC (By similarity). This subunit probably forms a homohexamer (PubMed:15668378). Interacts with VirB11 (PubMed:17038312). The C terminus of VirB4 also interacts with the periplasmic portions of VirB1, VirB8 and VirB10 (PubMed:17038312)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17038312"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22027007"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"The C-terminal domain is periplasmic (PubMed:17038312). The protein is anchored in the membrane, possibly by its N-terminal domain (PubMed:17038312). However, a cryo-EM structure of a conjugative E.coli T4SS suggests that this protein may localize to the cytoplasmic side of the inner membrane (Probable). Localizes to multiple foci around the bacterial cell perimeter during lateral attachment to plant cells (PubMed:22027007)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12177443"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17038312"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8152380"}],"value":"Cell inner membrane","id":"SL-0037"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12177443"}],"value":"Peripheral membrane protein","id":"SL-9903"},"orientation":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17038312"}],"value":"Periplasmic side","id":"SL-9916"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the TrbE/VirB4 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":789,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Type IV secretion system ATPase VirB4","featureId":"PRO_0000022663"},{"type":"Binding site","location":{"start":{"value":433,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":440,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","featureCrossReferences":[{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"ligand":{"name":"ATP","id":"ChEBI:CHEBI:30616"}},{"type":"Sequence conflict","location":{"start":{"value":55,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":55,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"in Ref. 2 and 3","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"alternativeSequence":{"originalSequenc